For each word below, write ONE short sentence (12 to 22 words) that uses the word itself, spelled in full, in the sense given. Give it voice and mood: a question, someone speaking, a sigh, delight, a warning. No definitions; show the word in a moment of life. Answer as one JSON object mapping each WORD (as given, upper case) to its sentence. JSON only.

WHISTLE: the sound made by something moving rapidly or by steam coming out of a small aperture.
WIRE: ligament made of metal and used to fasten things or make cages or fences.
WORKER: a person who works at a specific occupation.
WORLD: everything that exists anywhere.
WORMHOLE: hole made by a burrowing worm.
WRAP: cloak that is folded or wrapped around a person.
